\ tools/dict-report.4 - walk the dictionary and print one line per
\ word: header bytes, body bytes, name. Used by Iteration 129 to find
\ out where a shell image's bytes actually go.
\
\ Header layout, from kernel.4's HEADER (and cross.4's "HEADER): a
\ 1-3 byte link holding the distance back to the previous name field
\ in the same thread, tag byte last; then a count byte with bit 7 set
\ as a marker; then the name, unpadded; then the body. kernel.4's
\ PREV-NFA decodes the link. FORTH-WORDLIST is a HASHED word list -
\ [thread count][head 0..n-1] - not a single chain, so no one chain
\ reaches every word and no chain is in address order.
\
\ Body extent is computed as "start of the next word BY ADDRESS's
\ link, minus the end of this word's name field", which works
\ because the dictionary is laid down strictly upward. That is why
\ this collects every nfa from all 32 threads and sorts them by
\ address descending before walking: following a single chain would
\ visit a third of the dictionary and compute every body extent
\ against the wrong neighbour.
\
\ Usage (i386 build shown; the same works for 8-byte cells):
\   printf 'S" pool.4" INCLUDED\nS" shadow.4" INCLUDED\n\
\           S" shell.4" INCLUDED\nS" tools/dict-report.4" INCLUDED\n' \
\     | ./relf32 kernel32.img
\
\ A body's bytes include the padding a data body carries before its
\ parameter field. The bytes before the first word - the two boot
\ calls and the locals cells - belong to no word, so TOTALHERE exceeds
\ the sum of the lines by exactly that much.

BASE @ DECIMAL
VARIABLE NFA
VARIABLE NFATAB
VARIABLE #NFA
VARIABLE TA
VARIABLE BE
: CELLB 1 CELLS ;

\ ABORT" is compile-only, so this has to be a definition rather than a
\ line typed at the interpreter.
: INIT-NFATAB 8192 CELLS ALLOCATE ABORT" dict-report: out of memory" NFATAB ! ;
INIT-NFATAB

: COLLECT ( --- )
\ Every nfa in every thread, in whatever order the chains give them.
  0 #NFA !
  FORTH-WORDLIST @ 1+ 1 DO
    FORTH-WORDLIST I CELLS + @ NFA !
    BEGIN NFA @ WHILE
      NFA @ NFATAB @ #NFA @ CELLS + !
      1 #NFA +!
      NFA @ PREV-NFA NFA !
    REPEAT
  LOOP ;

: LINKBYTES ( nfa --- n )   \ the length of the link in front of nfa
  1- C@ DUP 128 U< IF DROP 1 ELSE 192 U< IF 2 ELSE 3 THEN THEN ;
: SWAPC ( a --- )
  TA !
  TA @ @ TA @ CELLB + @
  TA @ ! TA @ CELLB + ! ;

: SORTNFA ( --- )
\ Descending by address. A bubble sort: it runs once over a few hundred
\ entries and the clarity is worth more than the cycles.
  #NFA @ 1- 0 DO
    #NFA @ 1- 0 DO
      NFATAB @ I CELLS +
      DUP @ OVER CELLB + @ < IF SWAPC ELSE DROP THEN
    LOOP
  LOOP ;

: WALK
  COLLECT SORTNFA
  #NFA @ 0 DO
    NFATAB @ I CELLS + @ NFA !
    \ The newest word by address - first in this order - ends at HERE.
    \ Anything else ends where the next word's link begins.
    I 0= IF HERE ELSE NFATAB @ I 1- CELLS + @ DUP LINKBYTES - THEN BE !
    NFA @ C@ 31 AND 1+ NFA @ LINKBYTES +
    BE @  NFA @ NAME> -
    S" W " TYPE SWAP . . NFA @ 1+ NFA @ C@ 31 AND TYPE CR
  LOOP ;
WALK
S" TOTALHERE " TYPE HERE START @ - . CR
BASE ! BYE
